## Control {{controlId}}: Ensure Actions of Individual System Users Can Be Uniquely Traced

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization ensures individual user accountability within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through unique identity attribution in all audit logs managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if signInLogsAvailable}}
**User-Attributed Sign-In Events:**
{{signInLogsCount}} sign-in events uniquely identify each user by User Principal Name (UPN):
{{#if logs}}
{{#each logs}}
- **{{userPrincipalName}}** — App: {{appDisplayName}} — Status: {{status}} — {{createdDateTime}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

Every authentication event is attributed to a unique Entra ID identity, enabling full traceability of user access to CUI resources.
{{else}}
Sign-in event attribution has not been confirmed.
{{/if}}

{{#if directoryAuditsAvailable}}
**User-Attributed Administrative Actions:**
{{directoryAuditsCount}} directory changes traced to individual actors:
{{#if audits}}
{{#each audits}}
- **{{activityDisplayName}}** by {{actorUserPrincipalName}} ��� {{activityDateTime}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

Administrative actions (role assignments, configuration changes, group modifications) are attributed to the authenticated user who initiated the action, with service principal attribution for automated processes.
{{else}}
Directory audit attribution has not been confirmed.
{{/if}}

**Accountability Controls:**
- Shared accounts are prohibited; each user has a unique UPN
- Service accounts use managed identities with individual attribution
- MFA prevents credential sharing, ensuring audit trail reflects actual user actions
- Session tokens include user identity, ensuring in-session actions are attributable

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine sign-in logs for unique user attribution, directory audit logs for actor identification, shared account policy documentation, and MFA enforcement records.

